{"route":"/docs/5.3/layout/utilities/","version":"5.3","renderedVersion":"5.3","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Utilities for layout","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"For faster mobile-friendly and responsive development, Bootstrap includes dozens of utility classes for showing, hiding, aligning, and spacing content."},"blocks":[{"id":"changing-display","type":"heading","en":"Changing <code>display</code>","level":2},{"id":"changing-display--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/display\">display utilities</a> for responsively toggling common values of the <code>display</code> property. Mix it with our grid system, content, or components to show or hide them across specific viewports."},{"id":"flexbox-options","type":"heading","en":"Flexbox options","level":2},{"id":"flexbox-options--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap is built with flexbox, but not every element’s <code>display</code> has been changed to <code>display: flex</code> as this would add many unnecessary overrides and unexpectedly change key browser behaviors. Most of <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/components/alerts\">our components</a> are built with flexbox enabled."},{"id":"flexbox-options--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Should you need to add <code>display: flex</code> to an element, do so with <code>.d-flex</code> or one of the responsive variants (e.g., <code>.d-sm-flex</code>). You’ll need this class or <code>display</code> value to allow the use of our extra <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/flex\">flexbox utilities</a> for sizing, alignment, spacing, and more."},{"id":"margin-and-padding","type":"heading","en":"Margin and padding","level":2},{"id":"margin-and-padding--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <code>margin</code> and <code>padding</code> <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/spacing\">spacing utilities</a> to control how elements and components are spaced and sized. Bootstrap includes a six-level scale for spacing utilities, based on a <code>1rem</code> value default <code>$spacer</code> variable. Choose values for all viewports (e.g., <code>.me-3</code> for <code>margin-right: 1rem</code> in LTR), or pick responsive variants to target specific viewports (e.g., <code>.me-md-3</code> for <code>margin-right: 1rem</code> —in LTR— starting at the <code>md</code> breakpoint)."},{"id":"toggle-visibility","type":"heading","en":"Toggle <code>visibility</code>","level":2},{"id":"toggle-visibility--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"When toggling <code>display</code> isn’t needed, you can toggle the <code>visibility</code> of an element with our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/visibility\">visibility utilities</a>. Invisible elements will still affect the layout of the page, but are visually hidden from visitors."}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/introduction"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/download"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contents"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/webpack"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/parcel"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/vite"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/rfs"},{"en":"RTL","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/rtl"},{"en":"Contribute","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started